    "plain_text": "Born in Rome during royal exile, Juan Carlos was educated in Spain under an arrangement between his father, Don Juan, and Francisco Franco. Franco designated him successor, and he became king in 1975. He then supported political reform, appointed Adolfo Suárez and accepted a constitutional settlement that converted the restored monarchy into a parliamentary institution.\n\nHis public standing was reinforced when he confronted the attempted military coup of 1981 in a televised address defending democratic government. Juan Carlos subsequently represented Spain abroad through decades of state visits and diplomacy. He abdicated in favour of Felipe VI after a reign of nearly four decades and later withdrew from official public duties.",
